# --- Character-swap plate suppression for the Hallway crossing (written 2026-11-07) ---
# Graded fault: Picture 1's face and wardrobe shipped, but the source's blonde hair
# survived from ~3.5 s to ~8 s (master frames 4.25 s / 6.63 s show P1's nose, mouth
# and blue collar on a blonde head; 8.20 s is already bald and correct).
# Hard evidence from the 15:21 policy-91 job
# (preview_6304387241898789799_1794035194310887700): the pass shipped
# .director_cache\source_remake_relay_video\v1_relay_861ef5fa9f0127f74570_0.000-8.500.mp4
# with source_identity_strategy = "original", so Relay received the untouched V1 and
# every hair tool in this module - the hair halo (the twin-tail-wig lesson: the box
# top excluded the crown, so the hair "was never asked about") and the crown split -
# stayed inert because H3_CHARACTER_SWAP_PLATE_SUPPRESSION has been unset since
# Round 49's manual-ComfyUI parity.
# Which gate this Shot's own box clears, computed with _closeup_gate_for_bbox:
# R2 [0.19839, 0.209259, 0.541017, 0.898148] -> width 0.343, height 0.689, area 0.236:
# no verified close-up gate (dominant needs area >= 0.72 AND width >= 0.80 AND height
# >= 0.82; head_dominant needs height >= 0.75 AND width <= 0.45), but the silent-listener
# band gate (area >= 0.050, height >= 0.25), which weakens only the head-and-neck band
# (45 % from the box top, i.e. y 0.209-0.519, plus the halo up to y 0.029 and x 0.14-0.56,
# clipped at protected R1's near edge 0.558) and leaves pose, torso and motion cues alone.
# blur_desat is the crown arm built for this exact symptom - "its own colour keeps
# re-seeding itself under Picture 1's hair" - with the chroma drain at 0.25.
# Roll back one step at a time: H3_CHARACTER_SWAP_HAIR_BAND_MODE=off keeps the face
# band and halo; H3_CHARACTER_SWAP_PLATE_SUPPRESSION=0 restores today's plate exactly.
# Both are read when Studio starts, so restart before pressing Preview.
H3_CHARACTER_SWAP_PLATE_SUPPRESSION=1
H3_CHARACTER_SWAP_HAIR_BAND_MODE=blur_desat
